ty. It features apical-basal polarity with apical secretory granules, and tight junctions that maintain polarity and regulate calcium-dependent saliva exocytosis triggered by parasympathetic and sympathetic signals (Ambudkar, 2015). This cell functions in coordination with contractile myoepithelial cells, which aid saliva flow through the ducts into the oral cavity (Khan et al., 2022). In mice and humans, acinar cell development relies on the transcription factor SOX2 (Emmerson et al., 2017), with self-renewal achieved primarily through acinar cell self-duplication and supported by progenitor populations during injury and regeneration (Aure et al., 2016).\")\n\n  Line 20516: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24646566\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002623 \"salivary gland acinar cell\")\n\n  Line 20517: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002623 \"acinar cell of salivary gland\")\n\n  Line 23344: # Class: obo:CL_0009005 (salivary gland cell)\n\n  Line 23346: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009005 \"Any cell in a salivary gland.\")\n\n  Line 23349: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009005 \"salivary gland cell\")\n\n  Line 25317: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0019001 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000313 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0007196)))\n\n  Line 26789: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_1000330 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000313 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001901)))\n\n  Line 26796: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_1000331 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000313 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002031)))\n\n  Line 26803: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_1000332 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000313 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001958)))\n\n  Line 26810: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_1000333 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000313 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_8600001)))\n\n  Line 29360: # Class: obo:CL_1001596 (salivary gland glandular cell)\n\n  Line 29362: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"HPA:HPA\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"NPX:PDR\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1001596 \"Glandular cell of salivary gland. Example: Serous cells, mucous cells, cuboidal epithelial cells of the intercalated ducts, simple cuboidal epithelium of the striated ducts, epithelial cells of excretory ducts.\")\n\n  Line 29364: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CALOHA:TS-1282\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_1001596 \"salivary gland glandular cells\")\n\n  Line 29365: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_1001596 \"salivary gland glandular cell\")\n\n  Line 32806: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4033005 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000313 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_8410043)))\n\n  Line 33948: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4042016 obo:CL_0000313)\n\n  Line 35051: # Class: obo:CL_4052048 (intercalated cell of salivary gland)\n\n  Line 35053: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30855909\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35799078\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36726292\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37724716\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052048 \"A cuboidal epithelial cell that is part of the intercalated duct of salivary gland. This cell expresses proteins commonly associated with acinar cells and displays calcium signaling characteristics similar to secretory cells, indicating an active role in the secretory process rather than ion reabsorption.\")\n\n  Line 35060: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052048 \"intercalated cell of salivary gland\")\n\n  Line 35065: # Class: obo:CL_4052049 (striated cell of salivary gland)\n\n  Line 35067: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30855909\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34147989\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36726292\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052049 \"An columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell that is part of the striated duct of salivary gland, characterized by basal striations formed by infoldings of the plasma membrane. This cell play a crucial role in modifying the electrolyte composition and concentration of saliva through active ion transport, particularly the absorption of sodium and secretion of potassium.\")\n\n  Line 35073: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052049 \"striated cell of salivary gland\")\n\n  Line 35194: # Class: obo:CL_4052065 (serous acinar cell of salivary gland)\n\n  Line 35196: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29383862\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32829674\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35343828\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052065 \"An acinar cell of the salivary gland, characterized by a pyramidal or triangular shape with a spherical nucleus and abundant eosinophilic zymogen granules. This cell secretes watery, enzyme‐rich fluid containing α-amylase, proline-rich proteins, and secretory immunoglobulins for starch digestion and antimicrobial defence. In humans and mice, serous acinar cell predominates in the parotid gland and to a lesser extent in the submandibular gland, where it exists alongside mucous acinar cells (Maruyama et al., 2019).\")\n\n  Line 35199: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052065 \"serous acinar cell of salivary gland\")\n\n  Line 35200: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4052065 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000313 obo:CL_0002623 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0013232)))\n\n  Line 35204: # Class: obo:CL_4052066 (mucous acinar cell of salivary gland)\n\n  Line 35206: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29383862\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32829674\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35343828\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052066 \"An acinar cell of the salivary gland, responsible for producing a viscous, mucin‐rich solution, thereby facilitating lubrication and protection of the oral mucosa. This cell is characterized by an elongated shape, clear cytoplasm filled with mucin granules, and a basally compressed nucleus (Barrows et al., 2020). In humans and mice, the mucous acinar cell predominates in the sublingual gland and minor salivary glands, while also being present in mixed glands such as the submandibular gland, where it coexists with serous acinar cells (Maruyama et al., 2019).\")\n\n  Line 35209: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052066 \"mucous acinar cell of salivary gland\")\n\n  Line 35214: # Class: obo:CL_4052067 (seromucous acinar cell of salivary gland)\n\n  Line 35216: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29383862\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35343828\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36726292\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052067 \"An acinar cell of the salivary gland, with a hybrid seromucous phenotype, co-expressing serous and mucous markers and producing a mixed secretion of enzymes-containing serous fluid and mucins essential for lubrication, digestion, and antimicrobial defense. Predominant in the submandibular glands of humans and mice, its differentiation and secretory gene expression are regulated by FGFR2b–MAPK signaling, driven by paracrine FGF7 from adjacent myoepithelial cells, which provides a key niche signal for seromucous identity.\")\n\n  Line 35219: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052067 \"seromucous acinar cell of salivary gland\")\n\n  Line 35223: # Class: obo:CL_4052069 (excretory duct cell of salivary gland)\n\n  Line 35225: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28192873\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31194408\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1007/978-3-030-35784-9_2\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.5772/intechopen.75538\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052069 \"A duct epithelial cell that is part of the excretory duct of the salivary gland, which transports saliva from the intralobular ductal system to the oral cavity. While primarily serving as a conduit, this cell may play a role in the saliva modification, contributing to its hypotonicity. In humans, this cell has a pseudostratified columnar shape.\")\n\n  Line 35229: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052069 \"excretory duct cell of salivary gland\")\n","metadata":{"matches":45,"truncated":false},"title":"serous demilune|demilune|salivary gland|CL_0000313","time":{"start":1778980191317,"end":1778980191442}},"id":"prt_e337b7c420013K90F7GDOl9dNj","sessionID":"ses_1cc84c72affeOb6fpmbQ2mqZhW","messageID":"msg_e337b58b1001VOTtAd46oU4Qi1"}}
