ectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0003359)))\n34988: \n34989: # Class: obo:CL_4052040 (tuft cell of stomach)\n34990: \n34991: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22527717\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38117182\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1101/2022.02.16.480779\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052040 \"A tuft cell that is part of the epithelium of the stomach. This cell is characterized by gastric chemosensation and immune regulation through IL-25 secretion, which activates ILC2s to produce IL-13, driving epithelial remodelling and tuft cell expansion. Unlike intestinal tuft cells, which are primarily involved in helminth defense and type 2 immunity, the tuft cell of the stomach is primarily involved in inflammation, metaplasia, and hyperplasia.\")\n34992: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4052040 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\n34993: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4052040 \"2025-02-12T11:24:56Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n34994: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38117182\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4052040 \"gastric tuft cell\")\n34995: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052040 \"tuft cell of stomach\")\n34996: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4052040 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0002204 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001276)))\n34997: \n34998: # Class: obo:CL_4052041 (tuft cell of auditory tube)\n34999: \n35000: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30379593\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32733896\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052041 \"A tuft cell that is part of the epithelium of the pharyngotympanic (auditory) tube. This chemosensory cell is often positioned near cholinoreceptive sensory nerve fibers, suggesting a role in neuroimmune communication. It detects chemical signals and releases neuropeptides, such as acetylcholine (ACh) and CGRP, which contribute to inflammatory responses that help protect deeper tissues from harmful