{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778980382902,"sessionID":"ses_1cc84c72affeOb6fpmbQ2mqZhW","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_EMPnA5TR4562eEP5F76zjOEr","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","offset":35230,"limit":140},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n35230: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4052069 obo:CL_1001596)\n35231: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4052069 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0035049))\n35232: \n35233: # Class: obo:CL_4052070 (dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell)\n35234: \n35235: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40475517\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052070 \"A bipotent progenitor cell within the human fallopian tube epithelium, characterized by the concurrent expression of epithelial (e.g., EpCAM/CD326) and endothelial (e.g., PECAM1/CD31) markers at both the cell surface and transcript levels. This cell has the capacity to differentiate into ciliated and secretory epithelial cells, as well as potentially endothelial/stromal lineages. Positioned at the apex of lineage bifurcation, the cell exhibits stem-like and endothelial features, representing an intermediate developmental state between undifferentiated progenitors and lineage-committed epithelial cells.\")\n35236: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4052070 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\n35237: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4052070 \"2025-08-12T16:05:47Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n35238: Declaration(Class(obo:CL_9900001))\n35239: \n35240: # Class: obo:CL_9900001 (serous demilune cell of salivary gland)\n35241: \n35242: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23209333\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:41686279\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_9900001 \"A serous secreting cell that is part of a salivary gland, forming serous caps at the distal ends of mucous acini in mixed glands. This cell delivers watery, enzyme-rich secretions, including alpha-amylase, through intercellular canaliculi between adjacent mucous cells to reach the acinar lumen, and in human submandibular gland expresses neuronal nitric oxide synthase.\")\n35243: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_9900001 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\n35244: AnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_9900001 \"GitHub Copilot\")\n35245: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_9900001 \"2026-05-17T00:00:00Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n35246: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23209333\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_9900001 \"serous demilune cell\")\n35247: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23209333\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_9900001 \"demilune cell of salivary gland\")\n35248: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23209333\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_9900001 \"serous crescent cell\")\n35249: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serous_demilune\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_9900001 \"Crescents of Giannuzzi\")\n35250: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_9900001 \"serous demilune cell of salivary gland\")\n35251: SubClassOf(obo:CL_9900001 obo:CL_0000313)\n35252: SubClassOf(obo:CL_9900001 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001044))\n35253: SubClassOf(obo:CL_9900001 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0046541))\n35254: \n35255: Declaration(Class(obo:CL_9900002))\n35256: \n35257: # Class: obo:CL_9900002 (basal duct cell of salivary gland)\n35258: \n35259: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37446355\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39346911\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_9900002 \"A basal cell that is part of the duct of a salivary gland, characterized by an undifferentiated phenotype and a position surrounding the ductal epithelium. This cell expresses KRT5 and is thought to act as a stem or progenitor cell capable of regenerating ductal and potentially acinar cell populations.\")\n35260: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_9900002 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\n35261: AnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_9900002 \"GitHub Copilot\")\n35262: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_9900002 \"2026-05-17T00:00:00Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n35263: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37446355\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_9900002 \"basal ductal cell of salivary gland\")\n35264: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_9900002 \"basal duct cell of salivary gland\")\n35265: SubClassOf(obo:CL_9900002 obo:CL_0000646)\n35266: SubClassOf(obo:CL_9900002 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001837))\n35267: \n35268: Declaration(Class(obo:CL_9900003))\n35269: \n35270: # Class: obo:CL_9900003 (periductal fibroblast of salivary gland)\n35271: \n35272: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31213547\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39346911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:41411773\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_9900003 \"A fibroblast that is part of the stroma of a salivary gland and is positioned in the connective tissue surrounding the ductal system. This cell maintains the periductal extracellular matrix and can participate in immunomodulatory signaling, including induction of adhesion molecules associated with tertiary lymphoid structure formation in Sjogren syndrome.\")\n35273: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_9900003 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\n35274: AnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_9900003 \"GitHub Copilot\")\n35275: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_9900003 \"2026-05-17T00:00:00Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n35276: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39346911\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_9900003 \"salivary gland fibroblast\")\n35277: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31213547\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_9900003 \"immunofibroblast of salivary gland\")\n35278: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_9900003 \"periductal fibroblast of salivary gland\")\n35279: SubClassOf(obo:CL_9900003 obo:CL_0000057)\n35280: SubClassOf(obo:CL_9900003 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001044))\n35281: \n35282: Declaration(Class(obo:CL_9900004))\n35283: \n35284: # Class: obo:CL_9900004 (junctional epithelial cell)\n35285: \n35286: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14756251\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18973537\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39590534\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40723411\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_9900004 \"An epithelial cell that is part of the junctional epithelium of the gingiva and forms a collar-like band around the cervix of the tooth. This cell attaches to the tooth surface through hemidesmosomes and the internal basal lamina, expresses markers including CK19 and ODAM, and participates in innate immune defense while supporting rapid epithelial turnover.\")\n35287: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_9900004 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\n35288: AnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_9900004 \"GitHub Copilot\")\n35289: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_9900004 \"2026-05-17T00:00:00Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n35290: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39590534\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_9900004 \"JE cell\")\n35291: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18973537\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_9900004 \"cell of junctional epithelium\")\n35292: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19646321\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_9900004 \"gingival junctional epithelial cell\")\n35293: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7814753\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_9900004 \"DAT cell\")\n35294: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_9900004 \"junctional epithelial cell\")\n35295: SubClassOf(obo:CL_9900004 obo:CL_0002077)\n35296: SubClassOf(obo:CL_9900004 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001949))\n35297: SubClassOf(obo:CL_9900004 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0002227))\n35298: \n35299: Declaration(Class(obo:CL_9900005))\n35300: \n35301: # Class: obo:CL_9900005 (tuft cell of parotid gland)\n35302: \n35303: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23209333\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38358561\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_9900005 \"A tuft cell that is part of the epithelium of the parotid gland and is localized to the ductal compartment rather than acini. This rare POU2F3-positive epithelial cell is expected to have chemosensory functions consistent with tuft cells in other tissues.\")\n35304: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_9900005 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\n35305: AnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_9900005 \"GitHub Copilot\")\n35306: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_9900005 \"2026-05-17T00:00:00Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n35307: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:3284416\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38358561\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_9900005 \"parotid gland tuft cell\")\n35308: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18062147\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23209333\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_9900005 \"brush cell of parotid gland\")\n35309: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_9900005 \"tuft cell of parotid gland\")\n35310: SubClassOf(obo:CL_9900005 obo:CL_0002204)\n35311: SubClassOf(obo:CL_9900005 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001831))\n35312: \n35313: Declaration(Class(obo:CL_9900006))\n35314: \n35315: # Class: obo:CL_9900006 (tuft cell of sublingual gland)\n35316: \n35317: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23209333\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38358561\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_9900006 \"A tuft cell that is part of the epithelium of the sublingual gland and is localized to the ductal compartment. This POU2F3-positive epithelial cell is expected to have chemosensory and immune-regulatory functions consistent with tuft cells in other salivary glands.\")\n35318: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_9900006 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\n35319: AnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_9900006 \"GitHub Copilot\")\n35320: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_9900006 \"2026-05-17T00:00:00Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n35321: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:8874101\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38358561\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_9900006 \"sublingual gland tuft cell\")\n35322: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18062147\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23209333\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_9900006 \"brush cell of sublingual gland\")\n35323: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_9900006 \"tuft cell of sublingual gland\")\n35324: SubClassOf(obo:CL_9900006 obo:CL_0002204)\n35325: SubClassOf(obo:CL_9900006 obo:CL_0002251)\n35326: SubClassOf(obo:CL_9900006 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001832))\n35327: \n35328: Declaration(Class(obo:CL_9900007))\n35329: \n35330: # Class: obo:CL_9900007 (ionocyte of salivary gland)\n35331: \n35332: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30069044\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38358561\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39346911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:41721487\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_9900007 \"An ionocyte that is part of a salivary gland and is localized to the ductal compartment on the luminal side. This specialized epithelial cell is characterized by expression of FOXI1, abundant mitochondria, and ion transport functions that contribute to maintenance of osmotic pressure in the salivary gland environment.\")\n35333: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_9900007 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\n35334: AnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_9900007 \"GitHub Copilot\")\n35335: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_9900007 \"2026-05-17T00:00:00Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n35336: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_9900007 \"ionocyte of salivary gland\")\n35337: SubClassOf(obo:CL_9900007 obo:CL_0005006)\n35338: SubClassOf(obo:CL_9900007 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001044))\n35339: \n35340: Declaration(Class(obo:CL_9900008))\n35341: \n35342: # Class: obo:CL_9900008 (myoepithelial cell of salivary gland)\n35343: \n35344: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23209333\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39346911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40837863\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:41271704\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_9900008 \"A myoepithelial cell that is part of a salivary gland and is positioned between the basal lamina and adjacent secretory or ductal epithelial cells around acini and intercalated ducts. This contractile cell expresses markers including alpha-smooth muscle actin and helps expel saliva from secretory units into the ductal system.\")\n35345: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_9900008 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\n35346: AnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_9900008 \"GitHub Copilot\")\n35347: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_9900008 \"2026-05-17T00:00:00Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n35348: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23209333\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39346911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:8155903\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_9900008 \"salivary gland myoepithelial cell\")\n35349: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40837863\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1007/978-3-030-72029-2_4\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_9900008 \"salivary myoepithelial cell\")\n35350: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26015726\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27721614\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38273256\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_9900008 \"basket cell of salivary gland\")\n35351: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_9900008 \"myoepithelial cell of salivary gland\")\n35352: SubClassOf(obo:CL_9900008 obo:CL_0000185)\n35353: SubClassOf(obo:CL_9900008 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001044))\n35354: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40475517\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4052070 \"unclassified fallopian tube progenitor\")\n35355: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35320732\") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_4052070 \"non-ciliated secretory epithelial cell 2-1 (NCSE2-1 cells)\")\n35356: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35320732\") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_4052070 \"non-ciliated secretory epithelial cell 2-2 (NCSE2-2 cells)\")\n35357: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052070 \"dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell\")\n35358: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4052070 obo:CL_0011026)\n35359: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4052070 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_8600124))\n35360: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4052070 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_9606))\n35361: \n35362: # Class: obo:CL_4052071 (quiescent fibroblast)\n35363: \n35364: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21049082\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35701396\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40538750\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Fibroblast\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1038/s41427-020-0226-7\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052071 \"A fibroblast in a quiescent state, characterized by a smaller, spindle-shaped morphology with a relatively small cytoplasm, modest rough endoplasmic reticulum and condensed chromatin. Despite low proliferation and contractility, it maintains high metabolic activity for extracellular-matrix homeostasis through continuous matrix protein turnover and mechanosensitive signaling. This cell can rapidly differentiate into contractile myofibroblasts under injury or inflammatory cues to drive tissue repair.\")\n35365: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4052071 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\n35366: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4052071 \"2025-08-13T15:42:37Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n35367: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22529592\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4052071 \"inactive fibroblast\")\n35368: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID: 35701396\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4052071 \"Historically, quiescent fibroblasts in uninjured tissues were often called “fibrocytes”, but this distinction faded over time, and the term “fibroblast” came to be used universally, regardless of activation state. Fibrocyte has been repurposed to describe a distinct population of bone marrow–derived, circulating cells that home to sites of injury and contribute to tissue repair and fibrosis.\")\n35369: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052071 \"quiescent fibroblast\")\n\n(Showing lines 35230-35369 of 36127. Use offset=35370 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"SubClassOf(obo:CL_4052069 obo:CL_1001596)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4052069 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0035049))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_4052070 (dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40475517\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052070 \"A bipotent progenitor cell within the human fallopian tube epithelium, characterized by the concurrent expression of epithelial (e.g., EpCAM/CD326) and endothelial (e.g., PECAM1/CD31) markers at both the cell surface and transcript levels. This cell has the capacity to differentiate into ciliated and secretory epithelial cells, as well as potentially endothelial/stromal lineages. Positioned at the apex of lineage bifurcation, the cell exhibits stem-like and endothelial features, representing an intermediate developmental state between undifferentiated progenitors and lineage-committed epithelial cells.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4052070 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4052070 \"2025-08-12T16:05:47Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nDeclaration(Class(obo:CL_9900001))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_9900001 (serous demilune cell of salivary gland)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23209333\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:41686279\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_9900001 \"A serous secreting cell that is part of a salivary gland, forming serous caps at the distal ends of mucous acini in mixed glands. This cell delivers watery, enzyme-rich secretions, including alpha-amylase, through intercellular canaliculi between adjacent mucous cells to reach the acinar lumen, and in human submandibular gland expresses neuronal nitric oxide synthase.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_9900001 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_9900001 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_9900001 \"2026-05-17T00:00:00Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23209333\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_9900001 \"serous demilune cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23209333\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_9900001 \"demilune cell of salivary gland\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23209333\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_9900001 \"serous crescent cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serous_demilune\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_9900001 \"Crescents of Giannuzzi\")","truncated":true,"loaded":[]},"title":"src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","time":{"start":1778980382766,"end":1778980382898}},"id":"prt_e337e6824001NI5YUxk9L9joKX","sessionID":"ses_1cc84c72a