{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778980469226,"sessionID":"ses_1cc84c72affeOb6fpmbQ2mqZhW","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_PAhKO4Rt8OgQrWwojJqGkwsj","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Implemented the requested ontology additions for issue #3597 locally and committed the ontology changes. Please see PR #<NN> for review.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Implemented a set of new mouth and salivary gland cell type terms requested in issue #3597.\n+\n+Added new terms:\n+- `CL_9900001` serous demilune cell of salivary gland\n+- `CL_9900002` basal duct cell of salivary gland\n+- `CL_9900003` periductal fibroblast of salivary gland\n+- `CL_9900004` junctional epithelial cell\n+- `CL_9900005` tuft cell of parotid gland\n+- `CL_9900006` tuft cell of sublingual gland\n+- `CL_9900007` ionocyte of salivary gland\n+- `CL_9900008` myoepithelial cell of salivary gland\n+\n+What I changed:\n+- Added labels, text definitions, cited synonyms, contributor ORCID, creator, timestamps, and issue links for each new class.\n+- Used conservative modeling with asserted parentage and `part_of` restrictions aligned to existing salivary gland patterns already present in `cl-edit.owl`.\n+- Added function-related axioms only where they were directly supported by the issue text and existing local modeling patterns.\n+\n+Rationale:\n+- The imported issue body bundled multiple clearly specified new-term requests under issue #3597.\n+- Existing local ontology content already included related salivary gland classes such as tuft cell of submandibular gland, salivary gland acinar cell subclasses, and salivary gland duct cell types, so these additions were modeled to stay consistent with that local structure.\n+- I avoided overcommitting to more specific logical definitions where the issue text was broad or anatomy-specific evidence w